The consensus remains solidly anchored on [J, 1], representing the complete set of ten uppercase English letters with zero reflectional symmetry (F, G, J, L, N, P, Q, R, S, Z) in alphabetical order. The objection regarding the recursive digit reduction of S (19 → 10 → 1) is conclusively refuted because S is the only letter between R and Z that can yield the prompt's fixed ninth value of 1. Furthermore, idealized letter geometry canonically assigns horizontal symmetry to K, leaving [H, 8] without any viable unifying shape rule for the remaining letters.
}

